        "original_id": "c6900519-2cae-5896-b2ba-24c9d34b71fd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: The Dukes of Hazzard, Moonrunners\n- People: Gy Waldron, James Mitchum, Denver Pyle\n- Characters: Briscoe Darling Jr., Uncle Jesse\n- Topics: character-name and concept similarities, bootlegging\n\nFacts:\n- Moonrunners is a 1975 film about a Southern family that runs bootleg liquor, and it stars James Mitchum.\n- Gy Waldron created the 1975 film Moonrunners.\n- The television series The Dukes of Hazzard was inspired by Moonrunners.\n- The works The Dukes of Hazzard and Moonrunners share many identical or similar character names and concepts.\n- Denver Pyle portrayed the character Briscoe Darling Jr..\n- Denver Pyle was known for playing Grandpa Tarleton on Tammy, Buck Webb on The Doris Day Show, and Uncle Jesse on The Dukes of Hazzard.",
